// Builds a vector from three scalars, one per channel, like a #(r g b)
// triplet whose components can be expressions. Figure 12 calls it as
// (vector y 0.09 (cos (round y y))). A vector passed in is reduced to
// the mean of its channels, as avgLum does.
node "vector"(r: scalar, g: scalar, b: scalar) -> vector {
	return float3((r.x + r.y + r.z) / 3.0, (g.x + g.y + g.z) / 3.0, (b.x + b.y + b.z) / 3.0)
}
